I've started working on a patch for NetHack 3.4.2 to make playing
alternate races more interesting.  So far, I've implemented Hobbits as
a playable race (#define HOBBIT), and added the ability to specify the
alignment and class restrictions for each race (#define
CUSTOMIZE_RACES) in config.h.  Each of these may be used independently
of the other, in case one wanted to e.g. experiment with different
class choices for the existing races without adding Hobbits to the
game.

Hobbits have the following attributes:

 * Can be Neutral or Chaotic
 * Can be Cavemen, Priests, Rangers, Rogues, or Tourists
 * Have infravision (inhereted from the existing Hobbit monster)
 * Can recognise tainted food (since Hobbits are such culinary
experts)

I've also added the corresponding Hobbit Zombie and Hobbit Mummy
monsters to the game.  The tiles for these aren't that great; I just
modified the existing Hobbit tile for the Hobbit Zombie, and the Gnome
Mummy tile for Hobbit Mummy.  If anyone wants to contribute better
tiles for these, it would be appreciated.

For the CUSTOMIZE_RACES option, I've set the default racial alignment
and class restrictions to expand the choices a little bit for each
race.  This may be changed to suit your preferences, of course.  The
default changes are as follows:

 * Elves, Gnomes, and Orcs may be Chaotic or Neutral
 * Dwarves may be Lawful or Neutral
 * Dwarves may now be Barbarians
 * Elves may now be Healers and Rogues
 * Gnomes may now be Rogues
 * Orcs may now be Cavemen


If there's any interest in this patch, please try it out and report
any bugs and make any suggestions for improvement you may have.  I
have more ideas aimed at better differentiating the races from each
other that I'll implement time permitting, such as shopkeppers of
different races with their own prejudices, racial artifacts, and maybe
even different class quests for each race.

